{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred","id":1354366,"title":"Is there any way to reconcile these two theories about the origins of the Kindred?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-11T08:28:33-08:00","id":1354366,"title":"Is there any way to reconcile these two theories about the origins of the Kindred?","content":"1. The Strix are the ultimate progenitors of all the Kindred clans (not just the Julii).<br /> <br /> 2. Each of the five clans (six counting the Julii) has its own origin as detailed in the First Edition clanbooks.<br /> <br /> Is there any way that both of these can be true? I never really understood convergent evolution, and it is strange that five or six different species would be so similar...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:34:55-08:00","id":1354368,"title":"","content":"Different strix created different clans with different people, at different times.<br /> <br /> The first edition clanbooks weren't exactly clear on origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:47:21-08:00","id":1354371,"title":"","content":"Is it important that both be true? Given the multiple origin stories for each Clan (2nd ed core has 3-4 origins per Clan) as well as the presence of Ventrue and/or Julii centuries before their relatively commonly accepted origins (as per Ancient Mysteries), it's pretty clear to me that the Clans are not supposed to have a definitive and known origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:55:11-08:00","id":1354373,"title":"","content":"1. A clan's origins may be components of their modern manifestation; a monster may have been created by one circumstance, but not have been recognizable as modern Kindred until the strix somehow intervened as well.<br /> 2. A clan may have not one but multiple origins. There may be more than one way to make a Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T09:27:14-08:00","id":1354384,"title":"","content":"Sure, there could have been seven different general types of life-drinking corpse (if you take the Julii myths as true you should include the Traitors), which the Strix modified to create the modern clans. Maybe proto-Daeva used to feed by touch like a psyvamp, and proto-Nosferatu used to eat flesh, and proto-Mekhet used to eat Essence, and so on, and the Strix modifications are why they all drink blood now. Maybe the first Daeva was in fact Lilith, aligning with that particular origin myth\u2014and the &quot;owls&quot; I\u0161tar bargained with were actually shadowy figures with golden eyes. Etc.<br /> <br /> That said, it's an intentional design choice in Requiem never to have a Single Definitive Canon on where vampires come from, so remember that this is all speculation. You're welcome to have it be canon in your games, but it's not going to get Word of Dev confirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:16:35-08:00","id":1354401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354384#post1354384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, there could have been seven different general types of life-drinking corpse (if you take the Julii myths as true you should include the Traitors)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget about the Pijavica, Akhud, Grettir, and Mikhaili.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:20:57-08:00","id":1354403,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> thank you!! That works perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:35:30-08:00","id":1354427,"title":"","content":"It seems pretty clear that the origins of Kindred will vary depending on whom you talk to (in-game and out), and that all are true--from a certain point of view. The most fun seems to be to say &quot;yes&quot; to any assertion of origin, and then let the ST decide the weighting.<br /> <br /> So Dracula *was* a new type of vampire, convergent to the existing crop, and etc. The &quot;clans&quot; are convenient groupings of vamps by general characteristics, and as bloodlines show even that is loose at best. (You can have a bloodline bane that is the same as another clan's bane, for instance.)<br /> <br /> For that matter so long as a given clan of supernatural creatures have the &quot;vampire class&quot; of banes, consumes blood and concentrates it into a blood-like substance, it can be considered a vampire and either a new clan or an offshoot of an existing one.<br /> <br /> Or the strix are just responsible and we can all go home. But what fun is there in that?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T12:59:27-08:00","id":1354433,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> true lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T05:23:11-08:00","id":1354555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred#post1354366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way that both of these can be true? I never really understood convergent evolution, and it is strange that five or six different species would be so similar...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convergent_evolution\" target=\"_blank\">Since you asked</a>....<br /> <br /> TL: DR, version - some creatures ressemble each other not due to common origin/ancestor per se, but because similar circunstances played a role in how they adapt to their enviroment.<br /> <br /> In the case, a number of weird occult events exist in the world of darkness that may cause a corpse to rise from the grave.<br /> Most also make them hungry for blood or more rarely breath, essence or one's sins/trauma/etc. That comes from <b><i>the world</i></b> and how it works with blood, human corpses and certain (un)auspicious conditions, not the strix.<br /> <br /> Strix have a have of possessing corpses. Kindred are corpses, but also far more resilient than your typical unmoving cadaver.<br /> So <b><i>some </i></b>strix might <b><i>have learned</i></b> what circunstances facilitate the spontaneous rising of dead and how to exploit/facilitate them, to get bodies that are more resilient and entertaining to play with.<br /> Except some of those corpses come back with their human side in control - meaning a strix must wrestle it for control, what is not cool. Bestial ones are more fun.<br /> The rest is story and divergences of opinion, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-12-2019, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T09:08:18-08:00","id":1354584,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> that works too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:07:18-08:00","id":1354654,"title":"","content":"I think parallel evolution is the more accurate term for the different clans, but I mince terms here. I think everyone explained - Requem and CoD in general are more mysterious and whatever works for your chronicle. If you want everything to be explained and it to work the same way I believe Masquerade is like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T13:22:07-08:00","id":1354655,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2826_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2826\" data-vbnamecard=\"2826\">mikerand</a> tbh I like it best when both World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness are explained and everything makes sense, but maybe that's just me. I really loved how in Dark Eras they explained exactly how the Fall of Pangaea happened, how it tied Werewolf and Mage together and they even gave it an actual date (around 5000 BCE). Plus I like historical stuff in general. If I was gonna run a game, I would make them like mirror images of each other: different creatures, but the same basic themes (Gothic horror with a lot of romance and a little political intrigue, plus some combat to keep guys who like that stuff happy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T16:30:26-08:00","id":1354694,"title":"","content":"One origin I\u2019d been toying with might be useful to you.<br /> <br /> Simply put, the Stryx\u2019s natural state is one of pure stasis. In their natural habitat, or what was their natural habitat, time simply does/did not exist. Kindred pseudo-immortality is an inherited trait from them. For whatever reason (the fall of Pangea or Atlantis, intervention by the God-Machine, pure curiosity, whatever) they deemed it necessary to enter the Prime Reality of the WoD. Kindred were created possibly larval forms of the Stryx, or necessary chimeric man/monster organisms whose spiritual resonances allowed entry into a reality subject to the flow of time. The process was messy, as creatures who exist outside of time would have no concept of its mechanics. <br /> <br /> The end result was the creation of the proto-Kindred, clanless entities of both physical and spiritual ilk, emerging at various points along the convolutions of time. Whether larval Stryx or anchors between planes, the end result was what would be clan progenitors. The capacity for evolution is an inherited trait from the Man, something the Stryx didn\u2019t anticipate. Those who appeared in ancient times have had millennia to expand, procreate and evolve. Others who came later, or perhaps are yet to come, have not. Were Dracula or Longinus truly cursed by divine forces, or were they simply at the wrong place at the wrong time when the Stryx asserted themselves on our reality? Would they have eventually become clan progenitors of their own, given enough time?<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope this was helpful. It\u2019s a fun topic to play around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T21:00:42-08:00","id":1354715,"title":"","content":"The Strix like to say the Kindred are their fault, but if you believe them I know a Julii who'll sell you an aqueduct. The Owls almost certainly had something to do with the origin of <i>vampires</i>, but maybe not <i>all </i>vampires...and whether they made those vampires into clans (i.e., Kindred) is deeply suspect.<br /> <br /> The Founders were the only clan -- as we would define that word -- with a story tying their lineage to the Strix specifically. Indeed, the Julii are unique in that regard, in that their origin was more or less agreed upon in the Camarilla: The accord between Remus and the Strigoi, if you believe those fragments from Macellarius. The other clans, including the Ventrue, have their own multiple choice origin stories, some of which involve entities like the Strix, many of which don't.<br /> <br /> As noted above, there are many more clans than the five. The Akhud seem to have Embraced themselves, for instance, and evidence suggests the Pijavica have something to do with werewolves. The [REDACTED] claim they didn't exist before the 19th century. They even have the documents to prove it (they love to show off those documents, those copies of copies of copies...) Their vaunted papers say nothing about owls.<br /> <br /> And some vampires don't have clans. The All Night Society doesn't see them as their own, and maybe that's where the Strix show their claws. Think about some of the oldest myths of vampirism. A villager dies of &quot;consumption&quot; then rises from the grave as a bestial corpse and eats her husband, and then he eats their children. Rinse and repeat. As breath drinkers, the feeding of Strix might have been mistaken for disease, so maybe they left a few accidents. Or maybe it wasn't accidental.<br /> <br /> Perhaps all the Strix did is form the idea of vampires. Kindred came later. No wonder they're so disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-13-2019, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T23:15:48-08:00","id":1354726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354715#post1354715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As noted above, there are many more clans than the five. The Akhud seem to have Embraced themselves, for instance, and evidence suggests the Pijavica have something to do with werewolves. The [REDACTED] claim they didn't exist before the 19th century. They even have the documents to prove it (they love to show off those documents, those copies of copies of copies...) Their vaunted papers say nothing about owls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does those [REDACTED] know that in the case of vampires, the more papers you have to back your claim the more likely it is that people assume you are lying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T00:45:09-08:00","id":1354732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354726#post1354726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does those [REDACTED] know that in the case of vampires, the more papers you have to back your claim the more likely it is that people assume you are lying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of trust is a big problem for the [REDACTED]. A <i>big </i>problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T03:41:58-08:00","id":1354744,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> love Catch-22.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know much about the Akhud. How did they Embrace themselves?<br /> <br /> I read about the Pijavica in Thousand Years of Night, but I don\u2019t remember anything about werewolves.<br /> <br /> Oh shit. You\u2019re an actual writer!! Awesome \u263a\ufe0f.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T05:54:02-08:00","id":1354753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354744#post1354744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t know much about the Akhud. How did they Embrace themselves?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the original VII book, it involved a pact with a &quot;demon&quot; called Shaddad, the king of &quot;Irem of the Pillars&quot;. It was written way before Mummy, so who knows if there is any connection between the Arisen's Irem and the Akhud's.<br /> <br /> 2e claims them to be the product of a blood orgy of diablerie and Embraces, either the line of kings or those who rose from the lifeless bodies which were touched by the madness of the debouched kings.<br /> <br /> So we have three version about where the Akhud came from- the Diablerie Kings of the Five Cities, Sireless vampires who rose from the piles of the dead, or the surviving mortal line of King Ahran of the Five Cities who later made a pact with a demon from Irem to fight vampires as vampires. The truth is, probably, somewhere in the middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T06:10:43-08:00","id":1354754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354715#post1354715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some vampires don't have clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Clanless vampires, I've always had the theory that the spread of the Clans and lack/rarity of Clanless or single-member Clann vampires means that truly spontaneous Embraces (i.e. no other Kindred involved, just rising up as a vampire for your own reasons) tend to force Kindred into the existing Clans. That would explain why the four old main Clans (i.e. not Ventrue) are spread across the globe despite lack of contact and land bridges between cultures. A particularly violent murder victim in a South American bog rises and becomes the continent's first Nosferatu or Gangrel, spreading that Clan across the Americas. Ventrue would be much less common due to being so much younger and less spread (as well as not being connected to dreadful circumstances around a death).<br /> That explains why the four older Clans have fully developed societies in the Americas long before the arrival of the Ventrue with the European colonisers, without the Clans having to predate the original human migration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T07:51:36-08:00","id":1354772,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> awesome! I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:30:34-08:00","id":1354796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354744#post1354744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a><br /> <br /> I read about the Pijavica in Thousand Years of Night, but I don\u2019t remember anything about werewolves.<br /> <br /> Oh shit. You\u2019re an actual writer!! Awesome \u263a\ufe0f.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, with the Pijavica the implication about their connection to Uratha is more overt in the Requiem core, but their amorphous bodies and their similarity to the Gangrel suggest something a bit werewolfy about them.<br /> <br /> And yep, I\u2019m a freelancer. That in no way means what I say is necessarily canon, such as it is, but it does mean I get to throw little teasers here and there...!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T12:12:40-08:00","id":1354802,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> thanks. I love teasers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And I'm definitely gonna check out the Pijavica again.<br /> <br /> What about this? What if the creature Echidna from the Gangrel Clanbook was a Beast (maybe an Eshmaki Incarnate?) and drinking her blood is what transformed the first Gangrel into vampires and gave them Protean.<br /> <br /> Sorry. Sometimes I get bored and I try to figure out stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T14:04:36-08:00","id":1354818,"title":"","content":"Wait.......<br /> <br /> Re-reading the core book's section about the Pijavica, they went extinct in the late 19th Century. The [REDACTED] do everything they can to prove they never existed before the 19th Century. Applying Occam's Razor...<br /> <br /> Goddammit how those goddamned things keep on cheating death?! It's, like, the worst death-cycle any vampire can go through (the Formosae don't even come close), and they keep on surviving against all chances? Goddammit, you goddamned Dragons need to stop opening goddamned jars containing unknown goddamned blood samples. That's how those goddamned parasites just keeps on going, goddammit! They haven't died- they evolved!<br /> <br /> Goddammit!<br /> <br /> (unless it is all just a weird coincidence and there is no relation between the events. After all, they do have papers to prove their claims.. like anyone would believe those goddamned papers..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T15:37:50-08:00","id":1354826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354818#post1354818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.......<br /> <br /> Re-reading the core book's section about the Pijavica, they went extinct in the late 19th Century. The [REDACTED] do everything they can to prove they never existed before the 19th Century. Applying Occam's Razor...<br /> <br /> Goddammit how those goddamned things keep on cheating death?! It's, like, the worst death-cycle any vampire can go through (the Formosae don't even come close), and they keep on surviving against all chances? Goddammit, you goddamned Dragons need to stop opening goddamned jars containing unknown goddamned blood samples. That's how those goddamned parasites just keeps on going, goddammit! They haven't died- they evolved!<br /> <br /> Goddammit!<br /> <br /> (unless it is all just a weird coincidence and there is no relation between the events. After all, they do have papers to prove their claims.. like anyone would believe those goddamned papers..)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just a weird coincidence (or for the Doylist explanation, Yossarian didn\u2019t remember that!), but honestly, never discount anything with vampires. You might be able to read a Pijavica origin into the [REDACTED], come to think of it, but you\u2019ll have to see their write up and decide for yourself.<br /> <br /> Oh! Actually, I can provide the tiniest spoiler, because it was posted on the blog. If I\u2019m not mistaken, this lady is one of them:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/AndreaPayne_SpilledBlood1.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/up...lledBlood1.png</a><br /> <br /> Take that as you will. Her name is Ida.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T07:47:20-08:00","id":1354889,"title":"","content":"I feel like this idea is emerging that vampirism is something that keeps popping up as a side-effect and waste product of various other arcane events and I like it. Vampirism as occult waste product","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T14:17:23-08:00","id":1354921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354889#post1354889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this idea is emerging that vampirism is something that keeps popping up as a side-effect and waste product of various other arcane events and I like it. Vampirism as occult waste product</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great way of putting it. Especially in contrast to the certain, self-important conceptions of vampires as a curse from God, or scions of the Mother of Monsters.<br /> <br /> Kindred: waste heat of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T14:28:31-08:00","id":1354926,"title":"","content":"Well, Blood Potency does rise spontaneously, which does indicate a more entropic nature to the process compared to other occult works. The spiraling way that a vampiric psych decomposes from Humanity to the Beast also hints towards that concept. So yeah, vampirism and entropy seem to walk well hand in hand, concept wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T15:24:40-08:00","id":1354931,"title":"","content":"It's not completely spontaneous. It's tied to periods of activity, while loss of Blood Potency is tied to periods of inactivity. Periods of intense activity increases Blood Potency even faster, as represented by buying with Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T15:49:46-08:00","id":1354932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354931#post1354931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not completely spontaneous. It's tied to periods of activity, while loss of Blood Potency is tied to periods of inactivity. Periods of intense activity increases Blood Potency even faster, as represented by buying with Experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;spontaneous&quot; means in that context &quot;happens without investing work&quot;. Vampire doesn't need to do much to cause Blood Potency to rise- they can accelerate the process, just like any system can accelerate the production of entropy, but unless the vampire is in torpor, Blood Potency rise on its own, and in order to reduce Blood Potency, vampires require going to a death like state- which is a state of &quot;reduced entropy&quot;, even though it means that that energy must go somewhere, or more exactly, the reduce their own entropy on the expense of the &quot;entropy of the universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it is spontaneous by definition. The fact you can enhance the process or toy with it does not contradict it. It still gives a direction to the &quot;arrow of time&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T15:59:36-08:00","id":1354934,"title":"","content":"YAAAAAAAY, I DID A HALP!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:12:55-08:00","id":1354937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354932#post1354932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;spontaneous&quot; means in that context &quot;happens without investing work&quot;. Vampire doesn't need to do much to cause Blood Potency to rise- they can accelerate the process, just like any system can accelerate the production of entropy, but unless the vampire is in torpor, Blood Potency rise on its own, and in order to reduce Blood Potency, vampires require going to a death like state- which is a state of &quot;reduced entropy&quot;, even though it means that that energy must go somewhere, or more exactly, the reduce their own entropy on the expense of the &quot;entropy of the universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it is spontaneous by definition. The fact you can enhance the process or toy with it does not contradict it. It still gives a direction to the &quot;arrow of time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lost, the process explicitly requires fuel that is not passively gathered. The natural state of a vampire is torpor with periodic bursts of activity from which an accumulative span can start. If you're active for any length of time, you have access to a source of Vitae, which is not the default state of vampirism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T01:52:05-08:00","id":1355149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354937#post1354937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost, the process explicitly requires fuel that is not passively gathered. The natural state of a vampire is torpor with periodic bursts of activity from which an accumulative span can start. If you're active for any length of time, you have access to a source of Vitae, which is not the default state of vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't wish to derail the thread for too much and I can't make a long post because I have a flight to catch, so I'll try to sum it up as short and simple as possible-<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;spontaneous&quot; I mean &quot;without performing work&quot;, but when I say &quot;work&quot; I don't mean &quot;without any effort&quot;- &quot;work&quot; in the thermodynamical context basically means &quot;energy with purpose&quot;/&quot;energy you can re-use&quot;/&quot;energy with a defined direction&quot;. It is the opposite of &quot;heat&quot;, which is &quot;energy you can't fully re-use&quot;/&quot;energy without purpose/direction&quot;. It is a very &quot;handwavy&quot; way to define it, but it helps. This is also the idea behind the Second Law- &quot;heat&quot;, that is, &quot;energy which is not work&quot;, is governed by entropy, while &quot;work&quot; is generally governed by forces and momentum. <br /> <br /> So when I say &quot;rise in Blood Potency is spontaneous&quot; I mean that it happens without the vampire actively working towards it- it is a byproduct of their existence and activity. Gathering Vitae, using Disciplines, and simply existing produce more and more &quot;occult heat&quot;, which represents - to me - as the rise of &quot;temperature&quot; of the vampire's occult energy. You can increase Blood Potency with experience and Diablerie, but we could also increase temperature knowingly- but, again, temperature is all about random movement of particles, things which happen without &quot;work&quot;, energy which is &quot;lost&quot; to the ever growing heat of the universe. Of course it requires fuel and activity- but that's the point of entropy. Consuming fuel and giving heat, energy which could only be partially harvested into &quot;work&quot;.<br /> <br /> As long as a vampire regularly feeds and exists, they increase in Blood Potency without investing any effort in doing so (that is, investing exp). As such, you could always assume that as long as a vampire haven't fallen into a torpor, that is kept safe and fed with the needed Vitae, they will have an higher Blood Potency than a younger one, hence directing the arrow of time- which further suggest an entropic process which happens spontaneously. Torpor is corresponded into &quot;cooling&quot; the vampire- which means that the excess &quot;heat&quot; they gathered goes to the surroundings. The whole concept of &quot;Blood Potency rises with activity and falls with inactivity&quot; further reinforce the entropic &quot;themes&quot; of Blood Potency, as again, entropy and heat increase by doing activity which is &quot;without purpose&quot;. Investing energy without doing work (or, at least, wasting more energy than actually using for the process in question).<br /> <br /> So that's the clarification, more or less. In the way I see it, vampirism is all about wasting energy, decay, and going down the spiral- all which are the expression of entropy, and Blood Potency is, essentially, the &quot;occult form&quot; of temperature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T03:44:37-08:00","id":1355354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354889#post1354889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this idea is emerging that vampirism is something that keeps popping up as a side-effect and waste product of various other arcane events and I like it. Vampirism as occult waste product</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. You get a number of strange arcane circunstances together, a corpse with life-stealing hunger and a degree of human memories will arise.<br /> The rest is either <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_of_truly_large_numbers\" target=\"_blank\">numbers</a> or the (once)human mind trying to give meaning/purpose to (improbable) chance or &quot;game the system&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-17-2019, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:04:52-08:00","id":1355660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1354889#post1354889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this idea is emerging that vampirism is something that keeps popping up as a side-effect and waste product of various other arcane events and I like it. Vampirism as occult waste product</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if you break a random Mummy Relic you get some kind of monster. If you break a random occult ritual--or it's insufficiently shielded--then you can get a vampire. <br /> <br /> Most would not survive, nor be stable, but some might!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:28:40-08:00","id":1355663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1355660#post1355660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you break a random Mummy Relic you get some kind of monster. If you break a random occult ritual--or it's insufficiently shielded--then you can get a vampire.<br /> <br /> Most would not survive, nor be stable, but some might!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about Deviants then in this theory? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:35:36-08:00","id":1355890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1354366-is-there-any-way-to-reconcile-these-two-theories-about-the-origins-of-the-kindred?p=1355663#post1355663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about Deviants then in this theory? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know enough about Deviants, but I'd suppose the are mostly derived from scientific/alchemical efforts. Which is a vigorous handwave for &quot;explainable magic&quot;. <br /> <br /> Oh. Here you go: if your occult mess results in a corpse it may return as a vampire-ish thingie.<br /> <br /> If your occult mess results in a live body it may be a Deviant.<br /> <br /> If it's not one of these then the individual may be in the process of purchasing a minor template. Or two.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}